<title>FRANCE: Saudi barley priced up to $154 - traders.</title>
<headline>Saudi barley priced up to $154 - traders.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Arabia's reported purchase of 500,000 tonnes of barley is priced between $152 and $153 or $154 per tonne, grain traders said.</p>
<p>Traders said earlier on Wednesday the kingdom had bought 500,000 tonnes of April/May barley but the deal was subject to official confirmation, expected later in the day.</p>
<p>Around four offers were considered in a Tuesday tender starting from about $152 per tonne, industry sources said.</p>
<p>Prices include both cost and freight.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5146</p>
</text>
